Package: libstereo-declare1
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: declare full side-by-side stereo windows and surfaces
 A small C library with which an X11 or Wayland program tells Stereo KWin,
 the compositor of Sparky Stereo OS, that a window or surface holds both
 eyes side by side at full size, the left eye first. The kind of content
 travels as the surface's wp_content_type_v1 on Wayland.

Package: libstereo-declare-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libstereo-declare1 (= ${binary:Version}),
         libwayland-dev,
         libx11-dev,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: declare full side-by-side stereo windows and surfaces - development files
 A small C library with which an X11 or Wayland program tells Stereo KWin,
 the compositor of Sparky Stereo OS, that a window or surface holds both
 eyes side by side at full size, the left eye first.
 .
 This package holds the header, the pkg-config and CMake files, the API
 page and one example program per platform.

Package: python3-stereo-declare
Section: python
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: libstereo-declare1 (>= 1.1.0),
         python3-xlib,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends}
Description: declare full side-by-side stereo windows from Python
 A Python module for programs that start or watch another program's window
 and cannot link C, such as a launcher or a game manager. It calls
 libstereo-declare, so it makes the declaration the C calls make: it tells
 Stereo KWin, the compositor of Sparky Stereo OS, that an X11 or Xwayland
 window holds both eyes side by side at full size, the left eye first.
 .
 It also finds the window of a game from the game's processes or from the
 state file wiz3D writes, and removes the declaration when the window goes.
